==Changelog - February 18th==
{{Collapsed section|18|CLICK HERE TO SHOW}}
'''25th Anniversary Event: 25 Years, 25 Mementos'''

* This year marks 25 years of RuneScape and 13 years of Old School, bringing the perfect opportunity for a brand-new anniversary event!
* Start the event by talking to the Apprentice Wizard Gary Grayzag in southern Varrock, and help him open a portal to the Realm of Memories, a place where you can see and fight versions of creatures from the history of RuneScape. Think you've been there before? Well, there are more memories now - including the retro Kalphite Queen in her 2004-style glory!
* New rewards, inspired by Tim & Crunchy and by the event itself, await those who complete the event:
** 25th Anniversary Helmet
** 25th Anniversary Skeleton Tabard
** 25th Anniversary Warrior Tabard
** 25th Anniversary 5x5 Hat
* Plus, mark your calendars for our upcoming Anniversary Livestream on February 27th 16:00 UTC, where we'll be joined by MMORPG, Zecookies and Megan!

'''Deadman: Annihilation Tweaks'''

* To complete the “Have Prissy Scilla protect your Magic tree” task in the Western Province Diary, you can now pay Prissy Scilla to protect the tree.
* Summoned thralls via the spellbook will now last twice as long if you have the Sigil of the Augmented Thrall unlocked.
* Deadman Chests for Artio/Callisto, Calvarion/Vetion, Spindel/Venenatis now spawn outside of their cave entrance, allowing you to attempt to loot the chests without constantly being attacked by the bosses.
* The Trinket of Avarice will now also loot bones from NPCs automatically.
* Your noted items will now stack as intended even if your Looting Bag is full when you have the Trinket of Avarice active.
* The risk calculation when attempting to enter a raids area is now based on high alch value, instead of grand exchange value. Accordingly, the required value has also been lowered to 500,000 GP from 800,000.
* Since parts of the Ruins of Unkah breach occur in a safe zone, the location has been removed.
* Breach NPCs will no longer spawn on water.
* The Deadman skull countdown timer for the 2am breach now shows the remaining time left correctly.

'''Sailing Tweaks'''

* The current restrictions for UIMs on the Cargo hold have been removed. UIMs will be able to use the Cargo Hold like regular Ironmen - no more limited capacity!
* We’d love your feedback! Should the colours of Steel and Iron cannonballs be swapped to better match their appearance elsewhere in-game, and should the same change also apply to Steel and Iron nails? Share your thoughts in the comments on the dedicated update post across our social media platforms.

'''Other Changes'''

* We've made some feedback changes to the music system improvements from last week:
** Your mobile and desktop clients will now remember their volume settings separately. Meaning if you're an audio-enjoyer when gaming at home but don't want the entire bus to hear you blasting tunes on your way to work, your mobile client will remember its own muted settings.
** We've made it even easier to tell at a glance which track you're vibing along to with a handy recolour - and yes you can pick the colour from the settings!
** The "now playing" text above the music list can be clicked to read the unlock hint and to add/remove the track from a playlist.
* Fixed an issue with right-clicking Eluned in Prifddinas to recharge crystals, they will now charge correctly.
* Resolved a host of Z-buffering issues:
** Clipping issues have been fixed for the following:
*** The Nightmare's flower visual effects
*** The Kalphite Queen's tunnel entrance
*** Upstairs in the Grimstone Dungeon
*** The cave where the Hueycoatl sits
*** The vines near the Gryphon nests
*** Pier floors of Port Sarim, Port Phasmatys, Lunar Isle, Rellekka and Piscarillius
*** Rocnar and Tok-Xil from the dungeon below in POH
*** The Large Orrery in POH
*** The Blue Moon Inn fireplace
*** The walls of the Civitas and Fancy Stone house styles through another floor
** Fixed some rendering and flickering issues for:
*** The shadows of the pillars in Tombs of Amascut
*** The shadows of Leagues Trophies in the POH
*** The Earthen Shield and the ranged larvae at The Doom of Mokhaiotl
*** Some visual effects inside the Scar maze during Desert Treasure II
*** The Elemental Guards from the Sorceress's Garden
*** The wall kit of the Fancy Stone house style
*** The exam room door in the Surprise Exam random event
*** The Kourend Sigil banners
*** Various assets in The Path of Glouphrie environment
*** Some staircases in Hosidius as well as Varrock Museum stairs
** The cape icons of the Skillcape Masters are now visible for Crafting, Woodcutting, Herblore, Fishing and Firemaking.
