==Deadman: Annihilation Tweaks==
'''We've had a few players reach out about the Deadman Finale with questions about the cape they'll be given, since its functionality impacts their preparations. To keep things quick, the capes you'll be made to wear in the Finale are bog-standard Team capes, meaning they won't possess strong combat bonuses like the Mage Arena II capes, nor will they have the ammo-collection effect of Ava's devices. Stock up on those bolts ahead of the Finale!'''

If you have the Sigil of Nature, you might’ve run into an issue where you couldn’t complete the “Have Prissy Scilla protect your Magic tree” task in the Western Province Diary. This is because the sigil automatically plants and grows seeds in farming patches, but that’s been sorted. You can now just right-click Prissy Scilla, pay her to protect the tree, and the achievement will be completed.

[[File:25th Anniversary Event- 25 Years, 25 Mementos! (7).jpg|thumb|550px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-02-18/paytoprotect2.jpg here]!'']]

In addition, we've got the following fixes:

* Summoned thralls via the spellbook will now last twice as long if you have the Sigil of the Augmented Thrall unlocked.
* Deadman Chests for Artio/Callisto, Calvarion/Vetion, Spindel/Venenatis now spawn outside of their cave entrance, allowing you to attempt to loot the chests without constantly being attacked by the bosses.
* The Trinket of Avarice will now also loot bones from NPCs automatically.
* Your noted items will now stack as intended even if your Looting Bag is full when you have the Trinket of Avarice active.
* The risk calculation when attempting to enter a raids area is now based on high alch value, instead of grand exchange value. Accordingly, the required value has also been lowered to 500,000 GP from 800,000.
* Since parts of the Ruins of Unkah breach occur in a safe zone, the location has been removed.
* Breach NPCs will no longer spawn on water.
* The Deadman skull countdown timer for the 2am breach now shows the remaining time left correctly.

We know that you'd have liked to see some of these changes sooner, and we can only apologise for the delay. There's been a lot going on behind-the-scenes that requires careful testing and consideration, so we haven't been able to fit as many player-facing changes in as we'd have wanted to. For now, make the most of these changes ahead of the '''Finale '''on '''February 21st''', and note that these improvements will carry forward into future Deadman events as well.

The Deadman: Annihilation rewards will be available to purchase from Nigel in Lumbridge Graveyard on the 25th of February. Note that you'll need to switch to Permanent Deadman worlds first, then to the regular worlds where your points will transfer over.

