==Sailing Tweaks==
The current restrictions for UIMs on the Cargo hold have been removed. UIMs will be able to use the Cargo Hold like regular Ironmen - no more limited capacity! We hope you'll enjoy these changes, and thanks for your patience as we worked on them.

In other news, the team is hoping to launch changes to boat combat very soon, so that we can start to tackle the problems highlighted around boat combat from the Sailing opinion poll. If you're not familiar with the changes yet, please check out <u>[https://osrs.game/sailing-in-2026 this blog]</u> for more information. During the development of these changes, we identified that the colour of cannonballs are a little confusing. Steel cannonballs look like they should be Iron, and vice versa. Not to mention that Steel and Iron Nails also don't seem to accurately depict their metal. 

We think this should be changed, please see the following picture for our proposal:

[[File:25th Anniversary Event- 25 Years, 25 Mementos! (8).png|thumb|600px|center|''If you can’t see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-02-18/cannonballs.jpg here]!'']]

We feel strongly that this change makes sense for the game and would improve the new player experience in particular. However, since the current assets have been in-game for quite a while, we would really appreciate your feedback on these tweaks before they are live. Would you be happy with these changes, or do you feel strongly that the current assets should remain the same? 

As this type of adjustment relates to art, it falls under content that we don't typically poll. However, do let us know your thoughts on it and we'll take it into consideration.

==New Failed Payment Service E-mail==
We're introducing a new automated service email that will be sent if a scheduled membership payment doesn't go through.

If you receive this message, don’t worry. It's a standard notification letting you know there was an issue processing your payment and guiding you on how to update your details if needed.

Payment issues can happen for many reasons, such as expired cards or bank regulations, and this alert is simply to help you take action quickly and avoid any interruption to your membership.

As always, please stay vigilant when it comes to your account security. While this email is a legitimate part of our account support process, phishing attempts do still occur and bad actors may attempt to fool you using this new email alert.

If you're ever unsure about an email claiming to be from Jagex, please keep the following in mind:

* We only send these notifications from '''no-reply@contact.jagex.com'''
** '''Attackers may still be able to spoof this address, however, it should be flagged as spam by your email provider in most situations.'''
* We will never ask for your password via email.
* Links provided in the email go to our billing page via the Jagex Launcher. If you have any doubt, do not click links in the email. Instead, visit the official Old School RuneScape or RuneScape website directly and review your account there.

Your account security is important to us, and this update is simply part of keeping things running smoothly.

